---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CapabilityGrid from "../components/CapabilityGrid.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Certael project status — Pre-1.0 evidence" description="See which Certael capabilities are available, in progress, or not yet independently verified.">
  <section class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Project status</p>
    <h1>Evidence before<br /><span class="gradient-text">production claims.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Certael remains pre-1.0. Interfaces and packaging can change, and the project will not call itself production-ready until every acceptance gate has objective evidence.</p>
    <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/violetweather/Certael/blob/main/docs/acceptance-status.md">Full acceptance record ↗</a>
  </section>
  <section class="section-tight shell"><CapabilityGrid /></section>
  <section class="section shell" id="version-support">
    <div class="split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Version policy</p><h2>Signed support decisions.</h2></div><p>Core and Agent verify a short-lived policy signed by a dedicated offline key. A filename or client claim cannot turn an unsupported build into a supported one.</p></div>
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Allowed</h3><ul><li><strong>Supported:</strong> current recommended release.</li><li><strong>Deprecated:</strong> protected launch remains available while operators schedule the recommended update.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Denied for new protected sessions</h3><ul><li><strong>Update required:</strong> version or protocol is too old.</li><li><strong>Revoked:</strong> exact release was withdrawn.</li><li><strong>Unknown:</strong> product or protocol is not recognized.</li><li><strong>Indeterminate:</strong> signed policy is unavailable or expired.</li></ul></article>
    </div>
    <div class="callout"><strong>Safe degraded mode:</strong> a compatibility-feed outage does not kill an already admitted match. It prevents new protected sessions until policy is trustworthy again. Explicit session and build revocations still apply.</div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Outstanding gates</p><h2>What remains.</h2></div><p>The current alpha is meaningful security engineering—not a universal cheat detector or completed production certification.</p></div>
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Reference integrations</h3><p>Executable Godot, Unity, and Unreal reference games must reject the complete adversarial suite against equivalent server implementations across the certified platform matrix.</p></article>
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Operational resilience</h3><p>Multi-replica PostgreSQL and Redis failover, recovery, chaos, and tenant-isolation results must demonstrate no double grants.</p></article>
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Scale and usability</h3><p>The 100,000-session, 24-hour soak, latency, and external under-30-minute integration targets remain evidence gates.</p></article>
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Signing and independent review</h3><p>Windows Authenticode, macOS Developer ID/notarization, protocol, cryptography, backend isolation, adapters, release pipeline, privacy, and documentation require production evidence and external audit.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
